PERSONAL PORTFOLIO — SOURCE AVAILABLE, NOT OPEN SOURCE

This repository contains the source code, design, writing, photography and
other content of the personal portfolio published at https://sritulasiram.my
(the "Work"). It is made public so that people can see how the site is built.
It is not released under an open-source license.

1. What you may do

   - View and read the Work, and browse the repository.
   - Fork and clone the repository on GitHub, as GitHub's Terms of Service
     allow, to view it.
   - Run a copy locally for personal study and learning.
   - Quote short excerpts with attribution and a link to https://sritulasiram.my.
   - Take general ideas and techniques from the code. Ideas are not owned; the
     code, text, images and design as written are.

2. What you may not do without written permission

   - Publish, host, deploy or redistribute the Work or any substantial part
     of it, modified or not.
   - Use the Work, its layout or design as the basis of another person's or
     company's portfolio or website.
   - Copy, reuse or republish any photography, design screens, mockups,
     diagrams, case-study text, biography, portraits, certificates or other
     content in the Work.
   - Present the Work, or anything in it, as your own.
   - Use the Work, including the photographs, text and designs, to train
     machine-learning or generative AI models.

3. Third-party material

   - The case studies describe work done at Cytron Technologies. The Cytron
     name, logo, products and any internal systems shown belong to Cytron
